'''Items''' in [[Path of Exile]] are used to represent not just a character's [[equipment]] but a variety of other game features. Items can be moved around between locations using the mouse cursor, including the inventory, worn items, stashes, and others, as well as on the ground. Not all types of items can be moved to all item locations. Different item types take a different amount of space in grid based item locations such as inventory and stashes.

Depending on their type, items can have attributes such as [[rarity]], [[quality]], [[item affix]]es and [[item level]].

==Loot items==
In Path of Exile, "items" usually refers to loot items. These are items that have a physical representation in the game world as loot. They are often dropped by slain [[monster]]s or [[loot container]]s. When a player commands their character to pick up an item, it goes into the character's [[inventory]] where the player can then make use of it. In [[town]]s or [[hideout]]s, items can be stored in the [[stash]] to free up inventory space. Items can be purchased from or sold to NPC [[vendor]]s. Most items can also be [[trade]]d between players.

===Equipment===
{{main|Equipment}}
Equipment categories includes [[Armour (equipment)|armour]], [[weapon]]s, [[jewellery]], and [[flask]]s. Rarity is indicated by text colour ({{c|normal|normal}}, {{c|magic|magic}}, {{c|rare|rare}} or {{c|unique|unique}}).

===Currency===
{{main|Currency}}
Currency items are used to modify other items, and are also used for trading or gained from vendors for selling equipment. They have a {{c|currency|light brown}} text colour by default.

===Divination cards===
{{main|Divination card}}
Sets of Divination cards can be exchanged for a certain item, and have specific drop locations. They have a {{c|card|light-cyan}} text colour by default.

===Quest items===
{{main|Quest items}}
Quest items are found on the ground like other items, or given as rewards for completing quests. They cannot be placed anywhere but in inventory or back on the ground. By default they have a {{c|quest|bright green}} text colour.

===Gems===
{{main|Skill gem}}
Skills in Path of Exile are granted by gems which are treated as regular items. The skill can only be used when the appropriate gem is socketed in an equipment item being worn by the character. Skill gems, by default, appear in {{c|gemdesc|blue-green}} text when on the ground.

==Other items==

===Cosmetic items===
{{main|Cosmetic item}}
Cosmetic items use a separate cosmetic tab for managing them and applies to the whole character instead of on specific items.

===Hideout decorations===
{{main|Hideout decoration}}
Hideout decorations and crafting benches, when not in use in a hideout, appear as items in a hideout tab. They can be right clicked from this screen to add them to a hideout.

